P3-P6.md`\\n\\nThe live app is valid at 309 modules. Basic Science P3–P6 is closed. Image work remains paused.\\n\\n## Governing context\\n\\n- Repository: `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix`\\n- P6 Basic Science closure: `tasks/2026-07-13-p6-bsci-guarded-merge-report.md`\\n- Social Studies brief: `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/docs/ARCHITECT-BRIEF-SOCS-P3-P6.md`\\n- Existing live Social Studies content: `p1-socs-01..15` and `p2-socs-01..15` in `app/content.json` (30 modules, frozen)\\n\\n## What the brief specifies\\n\\n- 60 new modules: `p3-socs-01..15`, `p4-socs-01..15`, `p5-socs-01..15`, `p6-socs-01..15`\\n- Nigeria-first / global-enriched topic map (NERDC BEC Social Studies P3–P6 backbone)\\n- 5 sensitivity rules (religion, politics, gender, ethnicity, history/conflict)\\n- 3 modules requiring explicit per-draft user sign-off: `p5-socs-07` (drug abuse), `p6-socs-09` (terrorism), `p6-socs-03` (gender equality)\\n- Terminology open questions in §8 — must be resolved by M1 milestone, all locked before M2\\n- Schema contract, DoD, milestone sequence (M1 pilot through M5), integration mechanics\\n\\n## Next safe action\\n\\nMuhammad reviews and approves (or amends) `docs/ARCHITECT-BRIEF-SOCS-P3-P6.md`.\\nOnly after explicit approval does Foreman receive dispatch for M1 pilot (`p3-socs-01..06`).\\n# Current State: AJAMIX\\n\\n## As Of\\n\\n2026-07-13\\n\\n## Current Truth\\n\\n- **P6 Basic Science and the full Basic Science P3-P6 arc are CLOSED at 309 live modules.** The approved Nigeria-first/global-enriched source `tools/p6-batch/p6-bsci.json` contains exactly `p6-bsci-01..15`. The guarded merge on 2026-07-13 moved 294→309, preserved every pre-existing module object and every non-module top-level field, passed the 15-module structure/hook/redundancy gates, passed the full app validator at 309, and proved idempotent. The approved general pulley phrase is `na'urar dabaran igiya`. See `tasks/2026-07-13-p6-bsci-guarded-merge-report.md`. Image generation remains paused by user direction.\\n- **P5 Basic Science hybrid: CLOSED 2026-07-11 — 15/15 modules, 294 total runtime modules.** New band (`p5-bsci-01..15`): environment/pollution, waste/recycling, skeleton/joints, pollination, rocks, acids/bases, materials/drawing instruments, vehicle safety (progression beyond `p4-bsci-20`), energy conversion, heat/temperature, simple circuits, magnets, nutrients (progression beyond `p4-bsci-21`), diseases/prevention, drug-awareness safety. One hook-lint defect found and fixed directly (`p5-bsci-13`: `kwai`→`ƙwai`). All uncertain terminology (skeleton/bone/joint, pollination/fertilisation, temperature/thermometer, circuit, magnet, nutrient-deficiency, communicable/non-communicable disease) handled via descriptive Hausa, none invented. All safety-sensitive modules (acids/bases, circuits, drug-awareness) independently read in full — adult-only handling, no operational/unsafe content, non-stigmatizing language confirmed. All 279 pre-existing modules confirmed byte-identical. Merged via `tools/p5-batch/apply-p5-bsci.mjs`. See `SESSION_NOTES.md` 2026-07-11 entry. **Pending**: image/diagram-needs manifest for this band (new standing request, not yet produced).\\n- **P4 Basic Science hybrid additions: CLOSED 2026-07-11 — 21/21 modules, 279 total runtime modules.** Six new appended modules (`p4-bsci-16..21`: temporary/permanent changes, plant/animal life-cycle comparison, digestion/teeth, sound, vehicles/safe tech use, nutrition/healthy growth) built and merged; `p4-bsci-01..15` confirmed byte-identical throughout (zero changes, per the standing ruling that all 15 were already approved). `p4-bsci-18`/`p4-bsci-21` kept as separate modules per explicit user ruling (digestion/teeth vs nutrition, avoiding one ambiguous term across stomach/abdomen/intestine). All structural, quiz, redundancy, hook-lint, terminology (`gatari` confirmed absent, `sandar da ke tsakiya` used for axle), and safety gates independently verified — full content read di