\n\\n- Do not touch git — `git status`/`git diff` has hung repeatedly and unpredictably in this repo (documented pre-existing risk, reconfirmed again during the M5 merge scope-safety check on 2026-07-07); confirm scope by direct file inspection instead of forcing retries.\\n- **Process note (user, 2026-07-06):** for future scope-safety verification of protected runtime files, prefer content checksums (e.g. `shasum -a 256`) over modification timestamps alone.\\n- **Network note (2026-07-07):** Codex dispatches can fail silently on transient DNS/network errors, producing zero output with no obvious crash signal — always check the `.jsonl` log for connection errors before assuming a dispatch is just slow or trusting an empty result.\\n- When re-running check scripts, invoke each `node tools/p6-batch/check-*.mjs` standalone — chaining multiple node commands in one shell call has produced spurious, non-reproducible syntax errors in this environment (seen with varying error text — sometimes an em-dash-adjacent console.log parse error, sometimes an unrelated \\\"unexpected end of input\\\" — always non-reproducible on standalone retry).\\n- **Gate-coverage note (2026-07-07, Slice 3, fixed in Slice 4):** the structure-check script did not originally enforce the 120-170 word `textExplanationHa` requirement from the brief. Fixed in the Slice 4 build — the assertion now covers all 24 modules retroactively. Standing lesson remains: \\\"all gates pass\\\" is not equivalent to \\\"brief fully satisfied\\\" — always manually cross-check softer requirements during review, don't rely on gate PASS alone as the sole signal.\\n- Standing lessons for any future AJAMIX content work: brute-force-verify any formula beyond direct arithmetic (the harness doesn't check real correctness, and can't even confirm a formula represents genuine reasoning about the stated relationship); a single-pass regex terminology substitution misses mixed-case variants; watch for circular definitions and duplica