ext step: Foreman content ruling only. Do not apply patches, merge, or start P3/P4/P5 work.\\n\\n## 2026-07-10 - Claude - P2 Basic Science hybrid patch CLOSED — 19/19, 272 total\\n\\n- Context: resumed from a completed Codex candidate (tools/p2-batch/p2-bsci-hybrid-existing-patches.json, tools/p2-batch/p2-bsci-hybrid-new.json, ai-system report) that I had no session memory of — verified the artifacts genuinely existed on disk (real, ~20-min-old files, consistent conventions with this session's established canonical map) before proceeding, rather than acting on the description alone.\\n- Independent content review (not just the report): read both artifacts in full. All 4 new modules (p2-bsci-16..19: plant needs, habitats, materials, clay/moulding) read as genuinely safe, topic-specific, correctly terminologized (no ƙarfi-for-solid, no invented technical nouns — e.g. materials module uses \\\"ba sa lanƙwasuwa da sauƙi\\\" instead of an unverified word for \\\"rigid\\\"). All 8 existing-module patches (01,02,04,05,06,07,12,13) verified as genuine objective-preserving enrichments against the live content — same core facts/examples preserved, safety/behavioral framing added; the 3 pause-touching patches (07,12,13) have their audioScript [PAUSE N] markers exactly matching microPauses[].questionHa and correct answers present in options.\\n- Ran the existing check-p2-bsci-hybrid-candidate.mjs script directly (didn't just trust its claimed prior run) — OK, 19 modules checked. Found and fixed my own invocation error on the within-module-redundancy tool (needs --file= flag, not a positional arg — my first attempt silently defaulted to scanning live app/content.json for both calls, which incidentally reconfirmed the P1 redundancy defect from the earlier task plus previously-unknown instances in p5-maths-13/p6-maths-08/09/11 — flagged, explicitly out of scope, not touched). Correct invocation: 4 new modules pass, 8 patched-and-merged modules pass (0 findings each).\\n- Found one