e outside of Time Machine (and this machine has no local snapshots available, so on this system deletion is effectively permanent).**\\n- No further cleanup actions taken without explicit checks going forward.\\n\\n## 2026-07-10 - Claude - P1 Basic Science within-module redundancy fix CLOSED\\n\\n- User request: \\\"what's the next step for codex to do\\\" — after the P2 Basic Science hybrid merge closed and the unauthorized-deletion incident was logged, identify and dispatch the next bounded Codex task; user then said \\\"Yes, write the brief and dispatch it to codex.\\\"\\n- Current stage: CLOSED. Superseded prior open item — re-ran `tools/p1-batch/check-within-module-redundancy.mjs --file=app/content.json` against the live 272-module file before dispatching (never trust stale memory) and found the actual defect was narrower than earlier session notes implied: only 5 modules had live findings — `p1-bsci-02`, `p1-bsci-03`, `p1-bsci-07`, `p1-bsci-09`, `p1-bsci-14` — each with one exact/near-duplicate sentence in `textExplanationHa` only (`audioScript`/`microPauses`/`quizQuestions` were already clean). The previously-logged ~20-module Math/Social-Studies redundancy list from earlier in this session no longer reproduced against the live file — it had already been fixed by a prior closure (`2026-07-10-p1-final-content-quality-closure-report.md`, see CURRENT_STATE.md) that this session's memory summary hadn't reflected. Always re-verify against the live file before dispatching, don't trust a carried-over defect list.\\n- Work completed: Wrote a narrowly-scoped brief (`tasks/2026-07-10-p1-bsci-redundancy-fix-brief.md`), ran M0 preflight (`codex --version` 0.144.0-alpha.4, `codex doctor` clean), dispatched Codex in the background per `CODEX_ORCHESTRATION.md` with report/output paths outside the repo. Codex produced a source-only patch (`tools/p1-batch/p1-bsci-redundancy-patch.json`, 5 modules, `textExplanationHa` only) and did not touch `app/content.json` or create any st